<onlyinclude>'''Social metabolism''' (or societal metabolism) examines the flows of materials and energy between human societies and their environments. It includes extraction, production, consumption, accumulation and waste.

== Explanation ==
A city imports food, water, fuels and building materials. Some become long-lived stocks, some leave as products, waste or emissions. Measuring these flows helps explain resource use and environmental pressures. Unlike the metaphorical use of metabolism for ideas, these flows can be measured physically.

